[{"code":"top_level_list_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":17,"col":5},"end":{"line":17,"col":16}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL LIST CHANGED","message":"`update` changes `model.cells` in place, but when the program starts it is\n`initial`, a top-level value.\n\n17|    Tea.sandbox\n       ^^^^^^^^^^^ the runtime hands `update` the model here\n\n8|initial = { cells = [ 0 ] }\n  ^^^^^^^ the top-level list is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nBuild `initial` where the program starts, so that its lists are new ones, or\ncopy each list it holds there with `List.copy`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the list."}]
